WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
Ever wondered who actually does what at U M B C?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.621
You’re not alone. Let’s connect the dots, from the president to

00:00:07.621 --> 00:00:10.392
the people who help with your graduate experience.

00:00:10.742 --> 00:00:15.123
Start with the president. She leads the university as a whole,

00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:19.504
setting its direction and bringing senior leaders together. Academic affairs and

00:00:19.504 --> 00:00:23.486
student affairs are two different parts of that bigger picture.

00:00:23.836 --> 00:00:28.687
The provost is the chief academic officer. Think teaching, academic programs,

00:00:28.687 --> 00:00:33.538
and the quality of education. The provost works with college deans,

00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:37.948
the Graduate School, and leaders responsible for other academic areas.

00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:43.100
A college dean leads a particular college. Within that college, departments

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.902
and graduate programs handle work closer to your everyday experience. Your

00:00:47.902 --> 00:00:52.704
supervisor, program director, and department have different jobs, too. They’re part

00:00:52.704 --> 00:00:54.450
of your academic home.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.622
The Graduate School connects graduate education across colleges. Dean Christa Porter

00:01:00.622 --> 00:01:06.444
leads it. Its teams work on admissions, progress toward graduation, academic

00:01:06.444 --> 00:01:12.266
advocacy and professional development, and operations. For graduate assistants, this also

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:14.912
includes university-level guidance and concerns.

00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:19.603
Now switch to Student Affairs, led by Doctor Renique Kersh. This

00:01:19.603 --> 00:01:23.943
division supports student life and well-being. Within it, the Dean of

00:01:23.943 --> 00:01:28.284
Students helps with difficult circumstances and finding support. That’s a different

00:01:28.284 --> 00:01:32.230
job from leading an academic college or the Graduate School.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.298
You don’t have to memorize every title. Tap a role below,

00:01:36.298 --> 00:01:40.016
see what it does, and explore its team. Then open a

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:43.734
question that matters to you to see what’s changed and what

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:44.748
still needs work.
